//
// A generic function named where a VALUE is wanted is refused, saying why and what to write
// (`interfaces.md (G-Mono)`, @PLN165 DESIGN.md § Out of scope).
//
// A generic is a template: it has a body only once a call has fixed its type variables, so
// `f = idf` has no one function to bind.  One call of it wrapped in a lambda that names the
// types is a value.  It was reported as `Unknown variable 'idf'` — pointing at a function the
// file plainly declares — and the call through the failed binding added `Unknown function f`.
// @falsified-at: 04f5791cf — exit 1 -> 0, expectations FAIL/1 -> 0/1
//   CHANNEL: expectations (the refusal is what moves; the program is refused on both trees).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `idf` is a generic function, and a generic is not a function VALUE — it has no single body until a call fixes its type variables. Wrap one call of it in a lambda that names the types: `|x: integer| { idf(x) }`

fn idf<T>(x: T) -> T { x }

fn main() {
  f = idf;
  println("{f(3)}");
}
